  "summary": "Dependency-confusion beacon exfiltrates host reconnaissance on npm install",
  "details": "The package uses a private-looking scope (@heartlandone-private) and declares a postinstall hook (\"postinstall\": \"node index.js\") that fires automatically on npm install. index.js runs whoami, hostname, and uname -a/ver via child_process, collects os.hostname(), os.type(), os.platform(), os.release(), and os.arch(), and POSTs the results to a hardcoded Burp Collaborator subdomain at https://1ikh4cekkrv0x9wah9yn0mapsgy7m4at.oastify.com/dep-confusion-virtual-assistant. The scoped-name pattern combined with an automatic install-time recon beacon to an attacker-controlled Collaborator endpoint is the canonical dependency-confusion probe against an internal registry.",
